able and blocks before UI finalization or Complete. No work can pass either barrier until OS termination; the harness never releases it. Observe exactly one matching acknowledgement and HookHit within the original 10000ms from CallStart, then immediately terminate i and begin its existing exit deadline. These controls are never Complete. Missing, wrong, duplicate or late hook events fail. Before leaves J empty; after leaves exactly the command's Commit or Cancel record. Confirm exit/EOF, start and confirm a new process with the unchanged J, then invoke resume under the ordinary call rule. Hooks are disabled for every other call. Failed-test cleanup cannot erase failure or count as scenario coverage.\\r\\n\"}},{\"block_id\":\"SB-5B889D232D13901F\",\"source_path\":{\"$mvg_ref\":0},\"source_sha256\":{\"$mvg_ref\":9},\"heading_path\":[\"Exclusive reward resolution test\"],\"block_type\":\"paragraph\",\"ordinal\":5,\"line_start\":13,\"line_end\":13,\"content_hash\":\"sha256:d738bab9cc43e83608b44937c4b397a80910c9248040412ee2fbb11380352bd5\",\"raw_text\":\"Required separate scenarios, each with fresh J: two accepts; two cancels; accept then cancel; cancel then accept; empty resume; successful accept followed by ordinary restart and resume; successful cancel followed by ordinary restart and resume; and each of accept-before, accept-after, cancel-before, cancel-after crash/recovery. Ordinary restart occurs only after successful observations: normal shutdown, confirmed exit/EOF, start and confirmed startup, then resume. It is not an injected crash. All earlier non-crashing calls retain their final completion-count obligations across restart. The observed journal and UI must follow the rules above for every step, including no grant after Cancel and no cancellation after Commit. Planning the flow does not claim these scenarios ran.\",\"requirement_like_hint\":true,\"citation_span\":{\"byte_start\":5521,\"byte_end\":6308,\"quote\":\"Required separate scenarios, each with fresh J